# Data Layer (Remote + Local)

## Backend
- API: DummyJSON (`https://dummyjson.com`), docs: https://dummyjson.com/docs/products
- Base URL from `--dart-define=API_BASE_URL=...`, default `https://dummyjson.com` (`core/constant/api_constants.dart`).
- Endpoints used: `GET /products?limit&skip&select&sortBy&order` · `GET /products/search?q=` · `GET /products/categories` · `GET /products/category/{slug}` · `GET /products/{id}`.
- POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE are **simulated** by DummyJSON (not persisted). Never claim persistence.
- No price-range param exists → price filtering is local, pure, and unit-tested.

## Remote data source
- Only class that touches `Dio`. Returns **models**, throws typed exceptions.
- Map `DioException`: `connectionTimeout|sendTimeout|receiveTimeout` → `RequestTimeoutException`; `connectionError` → `NetworkException`; `badResponse` → `ServerException(statusCode)`; JSON/type errors → `ParsingException`.
- Search accepts a `CancelToken`; cancel the previous one on every new query.

## Local data source
- Backed by `SharedPreferences`; stores raw JSON strings + `cachedAt` timestamp.
- Cached: categories (TTL 24h), first page of the default listing (TTL 10 min), last opened details, favorites ids (if the design has favorites).
- Not cached: search results, pages > 0.
- Throws `CacheException` when empty/corrupt.

## Repository strategy (in `*_repository_impl.dart`)
| Call | Strategy |
| --- | --- |
| Listing page 0 | Online → remote → save cache → return fresh. Offline/timeout → return cache with `isFromCache: true`; no cache → `Left(NetworkFailure)` |
| Listing page > 0, search | Remote only; offline → `Left(NetworkFailure)` |
| Categories | In-memory → local (valid TTL) → remote → save |
| Details | Remote → save; on failure fall back to cached item |
- Check `NetworkInfo.isConnected` before remote calls.
- Never call the network from widgets, `build()`, or `initState` without a Cubit.

## Models
- `fromJson` is defensive: `(json['price'] as num?)?.toDouble() ?? 0`, lists default to `const []`, nullable image URLs allowed.
- `toEntity()` maps API product → `PropertyEntity`. Never invent fields the API lacks; see reference §4 (field mapping).
